Subject: [PATCH 09/10] =?UTF-8?q?feat(input):=20hold-swipe=20touchscreen?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20gestures=20=E2=80=94=20move=20windows=20with=20a=20held=20sw?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ipe?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Press 3+ fingers, rest them still for a moment (~400ms), then swipe:
the dominant direction resolves to a discrete action instead of the
animated view scroll / workspace carousel. Default bindings (in the
example config) move the focused column left/right and the focused
window to the workspace above/below, like Ctrl+Mod+Left/Right and
Ctrl+Mod+workspace-arrow keybinds.

Classification happens at threshold-crossing time, libinput-style:
the tracker timestamps when the minimum finger count was reached and
emits HoldSwipe instead of Begin if the fingers lingered that long
before crossing the 16px movement threshold. No timers involved — the
distinction is pure event state, so it stays unit-testable.

- niri-config: touchscreen-swipe { hold { left/right/up/down { … } } },
  any action bindable per direction, unbound directions fall back to
  the animated gesture, absent node disables the feature entirely.
- The handler routes a bound HoldSwipe through the existing discrete
  grab (TouchSwipeGrab::new_discrete), inheriting the deferred
  pending_touch_action execution (seat-touch deadlock rule) and event
  swallowing from the 4-finger flicks.
- A quick 4-finger flick still wins when the swipe was fast; how long
  the fingers lingered decides which action set applies.
